    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Miguel Vargas** serving as our primary engine, carrying a strong 63.53 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Abbott, A (xERA 5.02) provides the necessary ceiling for our 5x5 Roto push, as his projected xwOBA of .381 suggests he is primed to capitalize on this soft landing. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) and **Kyle Tucker** (60.78) anchor the middle of the order. Despite a potentially tricky outing against Drohan, **Kyle Tucker** remains a mandatory start given his reliability, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** receives a necessary boost from his #3 lineup placement and favorable platoon dynamics. We are also banking on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.88), who benefits significantly from a platoon advantage against Gilbert, L, providing a high-floor utility play despite the challenging xERA of the opposing arm.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved the lower end of our outfield depth, specifically weighing **Luis Lara** (44.52) against the baseline. **Luis Lara** secures a spot due to the scarcity of stolen base potential within our current roster constraints; while his raw score is marginal, his utility as a speed asset outweighs the risks of the pending lineup uncertainty. **Wade Meckler** (42.25) also makes the cut despite a brutal assignment against deGrom. While deGrom remains an elite arm (xERA 3.13), **Wade Meckler**\u2019s projected leadoff role and platoon advantage offer a path to plate appearances and base-running opportunities that we cannot afford to leave on the bench. \n\nRisks today are concentrated in our lineup pending status for several key contributors. **Andy Pages** (56.40), **Luis Lara**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Kyle Tucker** all await official confirmation of their order. While we have modeled for optimal scenarios, any late-scratch or demotion in the lineup will compress these scores. Furthermore, the presence of deGrom mandates caution; we are essentially betting on **Wade Meckler** to produce through volume and speed rather than efficiency. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** all inactive due to off-days, and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is tested. We are managing our game caps carefully, ensuring that only players providing tangible categorical upside\u2014especially in SB\u2014are occupying our active slots.",
